      "englishTranslation": "Reconciling 'Seeing Without Eyes' & Eternal Abodes (Part 2): Answering why 'Without hands and feet, He grasps and hastens; without eyes He sees, without ears He hears' (Śvet. 3.19) shouldn't be restricted merely to denying material-body parts while retaining spiritual limbs, Madhusūdana points out that the Lord's 'seeing and hearing' is simply universal Witness-Consciousness illuminating all sounds and sights—not ocular or auditory sense-organs! As for Purāṇic verses on eternal Vaiṣṇava realms, 'eternal' denotes relative endurance through intermediate dissolutions (avāntara-pralaya). Thus Brahman is proved Nirguṇa and Nirākāra.",
